      "writtenOn": "2026-06-29T17:58:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Deepa: Please make sure Yunqing or someone else checks this change.\n\nCould you please add a comment to explain why this function needs to align frame dimensions to a multiple of 2? I believe the reason is to ensure that `pix_to_bottom_edge` and `pix_to_right_edge` are even numbers. If that\u0027s the reason, then that should not be necessary when we are not subsampling in the corresponding direction, such as 4:4:4. So I think this change requires more thought.\n\nAnother question I have is that when we do want `pix_to_bottom_edge` and `pix_to_right_edge` to be even numbers, it\u0027s not clear whether we should round up or round down. Please also explain this in the comment. Thanks!",
      "revId": "9ceab5faa864a5310ac97e0d996bd3a58ecfc297",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "229f76df_dfb9000b",
        "filename": "av1/encoder/encoder.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 4297,
      "author": {
        "id": 8893
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-30T15:04:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you for the correction. Frame alignment is not necessary when chroma planes are not subsampled. We have corrected it in the new patchset. \n\nThe intent of aligning the frame dimensions is to ensure that the edge distances used for chroma planes remain consistent with the rounded-up chroma plane dimensions for odd frame sizes (e.g., `uv_crop_width \u003d (width + ss_x) \u003e\u003e ss_x`).",
      "parentUuid": "de309e6a_25f13640",
      "revId": "9ceab5faa864a5310ac97e0d996bd3a58ecfc297",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "225b4d5b_9a9603f3",
        "filename": "av1/encoder/encoder.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 4297,
      "author": {
        "id": 9545
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-30T17:53:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "See also my comment at av1/encoder/rdopt_utils.h:382.\n\nSince `ss_x` is `cm-\u003eseq_params-\u003esubsampling_x` and `ss_y` is `cm-\u003eseq_params-\u003esubsampling_y`, the `ss_x` and `ss_y` values are incorrect for the luma (Y) plane. The `pix_to_bottom_edge` and `pix_to_right_edge` calculated this way are incorrect for the luma (Y) plane (off by one) when the frame width or height is odd and the chroma subsampling format is 4:2:0.\n\nI think we should revert the `ss_x` and `ss_y` changes to the `set_pixels_to_frame_edge()` function and handle an odd `pix_to_bottom_edge` or `pix_to_right_edge` in `get_visible_dimensions()` instead.",
      "parentUuid": "229f76df_dfb9000b",
      "revId": "9ceab5faa864a5310ac97e0d996bd3a58ecfc297",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
